      "card_ids": [],
      "answer": "Ruling: The mutating creature spell is not countered. It becomes a creature spell (losing its target) and resolves by entering the battlefield as a new creature under your control.\n\nWhy: Rule 608.3b specifically carves out mutating creature spells: if the target is illegal, the spell \"becomes a creature spell and will resolve as described in rule 608.3a\" rather than being removed to the graveyard [CR 608.3b]. Rule 608.3a then states that an object resolving with no targets \"becomes a permanent and enters the battlefield under the control of the spell's controller\" [CR 608.3a]. So the creature simply enters the battlefield as a new permanent without merging with anything.",
