          "role": "user",
          "content": "My Saga has just triggered its final chapter ability, which is still on the stack. Is the Saga sacrificed immediately because it has enough lore counters?"
        }
      ],
      "card_ids": [],
      "answer": "Ruling: No. While the final chapter ability is still on the stack, the Saga is not sacrificed. The state-based action that sacrifices it is explicitly suspended until that ability leaves the stack.\n\nWhy: Rule 704.5s requires two conditions for the sacrifice: the lore-counter threshold is met **and** the Saga \"isn't the source of a chapter ability that has triggered but not yet left the stack.\" Because your final chapter ability is still on the stack, the second condition is not satisfied, so the state-based action does not apply [CR 704.5s]. Once that ability resolves and is removed from the stack [CR 608.2n], the next time state-based actions are checked the Saga will be sacrificed [CR 704.5s].",
      "sources": [
        {
          "id": "CR 117.1",
          "title": "Rule 117.1",
          "kind": "rule",
          "text": "Unless a spell or ability is instructing a player to take an action, which player can take actions at any given time is determined by a system of priority. The player with priority may cast spells, activate abilities, and take special actions.",
          "url": "/api/rules/117.1"
        },
        {
          "id": "CR 117.2",
          "title": "Rule 117.2",
          "kind": "rule",
          "text": "Other kinds of abilities and actions are automatically generated or performed by the game rules, or are performed by players without receiving priority.",
          "url": "/api/rules/117.2"
        },
        {
          "id": "CR 117.3",
          "title": "Rule 117.3",
          "kind": "rule",
          "text": "Which player has priority is determined by the following rules:",
          "url": "/api/rules/117.3"
        },
        {
          "id": "CR 117.4",
          "title": "Rule 117.4",
          "kind": "rule",
          "text": "If all players pass in succession (that is, if all players pass without taking any actions in between passing), the spell or ability on top of the stack resolves or, if the stack is empty, the phase or step ends.",
          "url": "/api/rules/117.4"
        },
        {
          "id": "CR 117.5",
          "title": "Rule 117.5",
          "kind": "rule",
          "text": "Each time a player would get priority, the game first performs all applicable state-based actions as a single event (see rule 704, â€œState-Based Actionsâ€), then repeats this process until no state-based actions are performed. Then triggered abilities are put on the stack (see rule 603, â€œHandling Triggered Abilitiesâ€). These steps repeat in order until no further state-based actions are performed and no abilities trigger. Then the player who would have received priority does so.",
          "url": "/api/rules/117.5"
        },
        {
          "id": "CR 117.7",
          "title": "Rule 117.7",
          "kind": "rule",
          "text": "If a player with priority casts a spell or activates an activated ability while another spell or ability is already on the stack, the new spell or ability has been cast or activated â€œin response toâ€ the earlier spell or ability. The new spell or ability will resolve first. See rule 608, â€œResolving Spells and Abilities.â€",
          "url": "/api/rules/117.7"
        },
        {
          "id": "CR 117.6",
          "title": "Rule 117.6",
          "kind": "rule",
          "text": "In a multiplayer game using the shared team turns option, teams rather than individual players have priority. See rule 805, â€œShared Team Turns Option.â€",
          "url": "/api/rules/117.6"
        },
        {
          "id": "CR 117.1a",
          "title": "Rule 117.1a",
          "kind": "rule",
          "text": "A player may cast an instant spell any time they have priority. A player may cast a noninstant spell during their main phase any time they have priority and the stack is empty.",
          "url": "/api/rules/117.1a"
        },
        {
          "id": "CR 117.1b",
          "title": "Rule 117.1b",
          "kind": "rule",
          "text": "A player may activate an activated ability any time they have priority.",
          "url": "/api/rules/117.1b"
        },
        {
          "id": "CR 117.1c",
          "title": "Rule 117.1c",
          "kind": "rule",
          "text": "A player may take some special actions any time they have priority. A player may take other special actions during their main phase any time they have priority and the stack is empty. See rule 116, â€œSpecial Actions.â€",
          "url": "/api/rules/117.1c"
        },
        {
          "id": "CR 117.1d",
          "title": "Rule 117.1d",
          "kind": "rule",
          "text": "A player may activate a mana ability whenever they have priority, whenever they are casting a spell or activating an ability that requires a mana payment, or whenever a rule or effect asks for a mana payment (even in the middle of casting or resolving a spell or activating or resolving an ability).",
          "url": "/api/rules/117.1d"
        },
        {
          "id": "CR 117.2a",
          "title": "Rule 117.2a",
          "kind": "rule",
          "text": "Triggered abilities can trigger at any time, including while a spell is being cast, an ability is being activated, or a spell or ability is resolving. (See rule 603, â€œHandling Triggered Abilities.â€) However, nothing actually happens at the time an ability triggers. Each time a player would receive priority, each ability that has triggered but hasnâ€™t yet been put on the stack is put on the stack. See rule 117.5.",
          "url": "/api/rules/117.2a"
        },
        {
          "id": "CR 117.2b",
